---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream a run's build and setup logs: everything the platform did before the test started.

Output: each line is `timestamp [stream] line`, where stream is `stdout` or `stderr`. The whole build is streamed, so expect thousands of lines on a real run. Grep the stream tag to narrow it, and read `[stderr]` first when a launch failed.

Examples:
  runs_build_logs {"run_id": "<run_id>"}

Each log line prints as one JSON object on its own line.
